 	 *
-	 * v161 settled the question decisively: flooding rows 200..680 white
-	 * BEFORE arm_vm_init painted a solid block on the panel (photo proof), and
-	 * the same flood in black AFTER it changed nothing. So the loader V=P
-	 * window at 0xC3401000 - the only mapping that ever reached this panel -
-	 * dies in arm_vm_init, and everything after it needs a mapping we build
-	 * ourselves.
+	 * The real fix lives in g0245d_fb_mark() (osfmk/console/video_console.c):
+	 * ml_io_map_wcomb() carves a FRESH mapping in kernel_map with
+	 * CACHE_ATTRINDX_WRITECOMB, i.e. non-cacheable write-combining, which is
+	 * exactly what a DMA-fed framebuffer needs. That needs kernel_map, so it
+	 * has to be called from machine_startup rather than here.
 	 *
-	 * v156 tried pmap_map_bd but then painted through the ml_io_map address
-	 * instead of the physmap address it had just mapped, so the mapping was
-	 * never actually exercised. v162 maps the splash range and paints through
-	 * EXACTLY that VA, then flushes the data cache, because physmap is Normal
-	 * cacheable while the panel is fed by MDP5 DMA straight out of DRAM - the
-	 * stores would otherwise sit in cache and MDP5 would never see them.
-	 *
-	 * Two blocks will be on screen if this works:
-	 *   rows 200..680  white  (v161 step 1 - proof we reached arm_vm_init)
-	 *   rows 700..972  white  (v162 - proof physmap now reaches the panel)
-	 * Only the lower block means the mapping still fails.
+	 * The white block painted above (rows 200..680, before arm_vm_init) stays
